 company also provides professional trust administration, investment management services, estate planning and administration, custody of securities, and individual retirement accounts. In addition, it offers brokerage and financial planning services, as well as assistance in various oil and gas leasing matters; and provides mutual funds, annuities, and health and life insurance products. Citizens Financial Services, Inc. was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Mansfield, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Randall E. Black | President, CEO & Vice Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $780,457 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 391 people. Revenue per employee of $287K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $90K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Citizens Financial Services, In is a small-cap financial services business with a $410M market cap on $112M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $35M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 1.00\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.30423428464838764},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 49% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(CZFS) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/CZFS_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111026041802_1794345482.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794345482.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Citizens Financial Services (CZFS) Upgraded to Buy: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024623/citizens-financial-services-czfs-upgraded-to-buy-here-s-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3024623","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793894402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","analyst_action"]},{"title":"Analyzing Citizens Financial Services (CZFS) and Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/analyzing-citizens-financial-services-czfs-and-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793754906.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Citizens Financial Services (CZFS) Q3 Earnings Meet Profit Strength And Credit Risk","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-czfs/citizens-financial-services/news/citizens-financial-services-czfs-q3-earnings-meet-profit-str","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793500423.02,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.897,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Citizens Financial Services (CZFS) Q3 Earnings and Revenues Beat Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3019333/citizens-financial-services-czfs-q3-earnings-and-revenues-beat-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-30193